---
import Layout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import JsonLd from '~/components/common/JsonLd.astro';
import { SITE } from 'astrowind:config';

const metadata = {
  title: `SUP Quality Testing Standards — CE, Pressure, and Durability Tests | ${SITE.name}`,
  description:
    'Technical guide to inflatable SUP quality testing: CE certification process, pressure hold tests, seam strength testing, UV resistance, and factory quality control protocols.',
  ignoreTitleTemplate: true,
};
const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: 'SUP Quality Testing Standards',
  description: metadata.description,
  author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: SITE.name },
  datePublished: '2026-07-27',
};
---

<Layout metadata={metadata}>
  <JsonLd data={jsonLd} />
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <nav class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-8">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-sky-600">{SITE.name}</a><span class="mx-2">/</span><a
        href="/research"
        class="hover:text-sky-600">Research</a
      ><span class="mx-2">/</span><span class="text-gray-900">Quality Testing Standards</span>
    </nav>
    <div class="mb-4">
      <span
        class="inline-block text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-sky-600 bg-sky-50 px-3 py-1 rounded-full"
        >Compliance</span
      ><span class="ml-3 text-sm text-gray-400">8 min read</span>
    </div>
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">SUP Quality Testing Standards</h1>
    <p class="text-xl text-gray-500 mb-12 leading-relaxed">
      Inflatable SUP quality is verified through a battery of standardized tests covering pressure retention, seam
      strength, material durability, and safety compliance.
    </p>
    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none prose-headings:text-gray-900 prose-p:text-gray-600">
      <h2>CE Certification (EU)</h2>
      <p>
        CE marking on an inflatable SUP indicates conformity with European health, safety, and environmental standards.
        For watercraft, the relevant directive is the Recreational Craft Directive (2013/53/EU) or the Personal
        Protective Equipment Regulation (2016/425) for life vests. CE certification requires: manufacturer declaration
        of conformity, technical documentation, third-party testing by a notified body, and affixing the CE mark.
        Products without CE marking cannot be legally sold in the EU. For SUPs, CE certification covers buoyancy,
        stability, load capacity, and safety warnings.
      </p>
      <h2>Pressure Hold Test</h2>
      <p>
        Every production board is inflated to 15-18 PSI (depending on rated pressure) and held for a minimum of 24
        hours. Acceptable pressure loss is &lt; 0.5 PSI over 24 hours at constant temperature. The test is conducted at
        20°C (68°F) in a temperature-controlled room to eliminate temperature-related pressure variation. Boards that
        fail the pressure hold test are inspected for leaks using soap solution and repaired or discarded.
      </p>
      <h2>Seam Strength Testing</h2>
      <p>
        Destructive peel tests measure seam bond strength. A 1-inch wide strip is cut from the seam area and pulled
        apart in a tensile testing machine. Minimum acceptable peel strength for fusion-laminated seams is 50 N/cm
        (Newtons per centimeter). Adhesive-bonded seams typically test at 30-40 N/cm. Samples are taken from production
        batches at regular intervals — every 100 boards or every shift, whichever is more frequent.
      </p>
      <h2>UV Resistance Testing</h2>
      <p>
        PVC samples are exposed to UV radiation in a QUV accelerated weathering tester per ASTM G154 standards. The
        standard test cycle alternates UV exposure (8 hours at 60°C) with condensation (4 hours at 50°C) for 500-1000
        hours total. Acceptable results: no cracking, no significant color change (Delta E &lt; 5), and tensile strength
        retention &gt; 80% of original. Boards rated for "coastal" or "tropical" use require passing the 1000-hour test
        cycle.
      </p>
      <h2>Drop-Stitch Thread Test</h2>
      <p>
        The tensile strength of drop-stitch threads is tested by pulling individual threads to failure. Minimum
        acceptable load per thread is 30 N (approximately 3 kg). Thread density (picks per inch) is verified by counting
        threads in a 1-inch square section under magnification. Acceptable density is 9-11 picks per inch for
        recreational SUPs and 11-13 for performance SUPs.
      </p>
      <h2>Temperature Cycling</h2>
      <p>
        Boards are subjected to temperature cycling between -20°C (-4°F) and +60°C (140°F) over 24-hour cycles for 10
        cycles. After cycling, the board must hold pressure and show no seam delamination, PVC cracking, or EVA pad
        detachment. This test ensures the board survives extreme transport and storage conditions.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
